{
  "id": "80517",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Quantitative Aspects of Electrolysis",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Electrical current is defined as the rate of flow for any charged species. The elementary unit of charge is the charge of a proton, which is equal in magnitude to the charge of an electron. The SI unit of charge is the coulomb (C), and the charge of a proton is 1.602 × 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "−19"
              },
              {
                "text": " C. We generally use current as a flow of electrons. Current is measured in a composite unit called an ampere (A), defined as one coulomb per second (A = 1 C/s). The charge transferred, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "Q"
              },
              {
                "text": ", by the passage of a constant current, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "I"
              },
              {
                "text": ", over a specified time interval, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "text": ", is then given by the simple mathematical product:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "tw7yytnyoqk0a7y",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "yitqrn511dtpcu4",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "z8cw260qkx30fm4",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "Q\\;=\\;It",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "When electrons are transferred during a redox process, the stoichiometry of the reaction may be used to derive the total amount of (electric) charge involved. For example, the generic reduction process:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "hgj85oovw8cnjuf",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "x89l6skw8gx3qki",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "ysx5jl2hd6fttgi",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Mn}^{n+}(aq)\\;+\\;n\\;\\mathrm e^-\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm M(s)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "involves the transfer of "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "n"
              },
              {
                "text": " moles of electrons. The charge transferred is therefore:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "slnuvdg0mh6vwes",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "ww8gvofopzzpngq",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "svfdxsl81pmu59q",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "Q\\;=\\;nF",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "where "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "F"
              },
              {
                "text": " is the "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Faraday constant"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The charge on 1 mol of electrons; "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "F"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " = 96,485 C/mol e"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "−"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2797101925",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1921886127",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": ", the charge in coulombs for 1 mole of electrons. If the reaction takes place in an electrochemical cell, the current flow is conveniently measured, and it may be used to assist in stoichiometric calculations related to the cell reaction."
              }
            ],
            "id": "ws3bds161qnnzxv",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "lemivnsgs5w9zos",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "u62228d74xl1ukp",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/8c/8cd9c36acbbedec8ba1b0d2257e025e8/Q_nF.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "500"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "3271584466",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "1443485843",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "In one process used for electroplating silver, a current of 10.23 A was passed through an electrolytic cell for exactly 1 hour. How many moles of electrons passed through the cell? What mass of silver was deposited at the cathode from the silver nitrate solution?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "im24mosp8fgmp8y",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We can use the given information and several conversion factors to calculate the moles of electrons:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "8dp0hk72hwjux5f",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "3oajd2pm3sz3537",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "qr8wwh5mmmslzr6",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "1\\;\\mathrm{hr}\\;\\times\\;\\frac{60\\;\\min}{1\\;\\mathrm{hr}}\\;\\times\\;\\frac{60\\;\\mathrm s}{1\\;\\min}\\times\\frac{10.23\\; \\mathrm C}{\\mathrm s}\\times\\frac{{\\displaystyle1\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm e^-}\\;\\;}{96,485\\;\\mathrm C}\\; =\\;0.3817\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm e^-",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "An alternative method is to combine the equations given above ("
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "Q"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "It"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "Q"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "nF"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") and solve for "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "n"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ":"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vr4c0afowyu62xk",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "fnps6ijjtnhtdih",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "qqshcdjnx505rty",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "n\\;=\\;\\frac QF\\;=\\;\\frac{I\\cdot t}F\\;=\\;\\frac{\\left({\\displaystyle\\frac{10.23\\;\\mathrm C}{\\mathrm s}}\\right)\\; \\left(1\\;\\mathrm{hr}\\;\\times\\;{\\displaystyle\\frac{60\\;\\min}{1\\;\\mathrm{hr}}}\\;\\times\\;{\\displaystyle\\frac{60\\;\\mathrm s} {1\\;\\min}}\\right)}{96,485\\;\\mathrm C/\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm e^-}\\;=\\;0.3817\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm e^-",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Because the silver metal is formed from the AgNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " solution, the reduction half-reaction is:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3xm8ervljnyoned",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "h22wjmr8trafujm",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "k2gy7gjew5giqer",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{Ag}^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm e^-\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm{Ag}(s)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "so 1 mole of electrons is transferred for each mole of silver. "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "uxop4kc5bctszlb",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We then use this relationship, the (previously determined) number of moles of electrons, and the atomic mass of Ag to calculate the mass of silver deposited:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "qh5ax0tc63oud1m",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "0k59ycte852firx",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "qs6axs0mq8mcu8r",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "0.3817\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm e^-\\;\\times\\;\\frac{1\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm{Ag}}{1\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm e^-}\\; \\times\\;\\frac{107.9\\;\\mathrm g\\;\\mathrm{Ag}}{1\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\mathrm{Ag}}\\;=\\;41.19\\;\\mathrm g\\;\\mathrm{Ag}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "589846199",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "294243686",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
